  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "With no prior experiments, the most critical uncertainty is whether a multimodal model (combining RNA + image) provides meaningful benefit over unimodal baselines, and what a reasonable 'simple multimodal' performance level looks like. Config_018 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, no aggregation, weighted fusion) is the simplest reasonable multimodal configuration: it uses the most straightforward RNA encoder (PCA, no learned parameters), a standard image backbone (ResNet-50), single-profile (no aggregation needed), and weighted fusion. This establishes a central anchor in the design space from which many one-parameter comparisons can be drawn in subsequent experiments: removing RNA (config_004) isolates the image-only baseline, removing image (config_046) isolates the RNA-only baseline, swapping the RNA encoder (config_019 scvi, config_036 scgpt) tests whether learned representations add value over linear dimensionality reduction, swapping the image encoder (config_021 ViT-L) tests backbone quality, and changing fusion (config_009 concat) tests fusion strategy. Starting here maximizes the number of informative follow-up comparisons per experiment under the limited budget."
}

